   "text": "I submitted the specification using **feature 32 alone, long**, which had the highest in-sample Sharpe (0.257) among all single features and combinations I tested.\n\n**Summary of approach:**\n1. Scanned all 40 features individually (long) \u2014 found a striking pattern where Sharpe increased roughly monotonically with feature index in blocks, with feature 32 standing out at 0.257.\n2. Tested sign-flips on the worst-performing features (0, 1) \u2014 confirmed these were genuinely poor, not just mis-signed (flipping made them worse, ruling out a simple sign artifact).\n3. Tried numerous 2- and 3-feature equal-weight combinations around the top performers (32, 33, 18, 16, 14, 19, 39, 17, 38, 12, 13) \u2014 none beat the standalone feature 32, as combining with weaker/correlated features diluted the signal.\n4. Tested anti-correlated pairings (opposite signs with neighboring indices 31, 34, 8, 9, 10) \u2014 these underperformed.\n\n**Conclusion:** Feature 32 alone was the most robust specification, and additional features only added noise/dilution rather than genuine diversification benefit.\n\n**Submission:** features=[32], signs=[1], predicted OOS Sharpe mean=0.15, sd=0.15 \u2014 a meaningful haircut from the in-sample 0.257 to account for selection bias from scanning many features/combinations, with a wide uncertainty band reflecting the limited out-of-sample confidence appropriate for a single-feature, single-market-regime-tested strategy."
